module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.MvPolynomial.Ideal
public import Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Aleph
public import Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Regular
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Algebra.AdicTopology.WeaklyAdmissible

/-!
# A countably indexed completion which is not adic*

Let `ω₁` be the first uncountable ordinal, let `A` be the `ℚ`-algebra on generators `x_α`,
`α ∈ ω₁`, and `y_{αβ}`, `α ∈ β ∈ ω₁`, modulo the relations `x_α = y_{αβ} x_β`, and let
`T = V(x_α : α ∈ ω₁) ⊆ Spec A`. The ideals `J_n` generated by the `(n+1)`-st powers of the `x_α`
all cut out `T`, decrease,
and are cofinal among the ideals cutting out `T`, so the completion of `Spec A` along `T` is
countably indexed; yet the inverse limit `lim A ⧸ J_n` carries no finitely generated weak ideal
of definition, so that completion is not adic*. This is Gabber's example, showing that the
hypothesis of **Stacks 0APW (1)** that `T` be cut out by countably many functions cannot be
dropped.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.IsCofinalVanishingSequence`: a decreasing sequence of ideals
  all cutting out a given closed subset and cofinal among the ideals cutting it out.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.IdealSequenceLimit`: the inverse limit of the quotients by a
  decreasing sequence of ideals, with the topology making each quotient discrete.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.GabberRing`, `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.gabberVanishingIdeal`
  and `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.gabberPowerIdeal`: the ring `A`, the ideal cutting out `T`
  and the sequence `J_n` above; `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.GabberCompletion` is
  `lim A ⧸ J_n`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isCofinalVanishingSequence_gabberPowerIdeal`: **Stacks 0APW
  (2)**, the sequence `J_n` is a cofinal vanishing sequence for `T`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.gabberCompletion_no_fg_isWeakIdealOfDefinition`: **Stacks 0APW
  (2)**, `lim A ⧸ J_n` has no finitely generated weak ideal of definition.

## Implementation notes

Both halves are ideal-theoretic. Countable indexedness of the completion of an affine scheme
along a closed subset is the existence of a cofinal vanishing sequence, and adic\*-ness of that
completion asks its associated topological ring — the inverse limit of the quotients of a
cofinal vanishing sequence — to be adic with a finitely generated ideal of definition. So the
statements here are about `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.IdealSequenceLimit` rather than about
the completion as an fppf sheaf.

The sheaf-level form of clause (2) is
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isCountablyIndexed_not_isAdicStar_gabberCompletionSheaf` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalSpace/CountablyIndexedNotAdicStarSheaf.lean`, and it is
deduced from the two statements here. The deduction is not formal. Clause (1) at sheaf level,
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isAdicStar_countableCompletion` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.CountablyIndexedAdicStar`, needs only *one* presenting ring that
is adic with a finitely generated ideal of definition, which is what the inverse limit of a
cofinal vanishing sequence provides. Clause (2) is the negation, so it needs the converse —
that *every* ring presenting the completion is the inverse limit of a cofinal vanishing
sequence, up to isomorphism of topological rings. That is the implication (4) ⟹ (1) of
Stacks 0AIC for a `AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.WeakIdealColimitPresentation`, now
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.exists_continuous_ringEquiv_of_isPresentingRing`, together with
the transport of "adic with a finitely generated ideal of definition" along such an
isomorphism, now `TopologicalRing.exists_fg_isIdealOfDefinition_of_ringEquiv`.

The absence of a finitely generated *weak* ideal of definition is stronger than the absence of a
finitely generated ideal of definition, an ideal of definition being in particular a weak one, so
it is this stronger statement that is proved.

The base field is taken to be `ℚ`, where the source allows an arbitrary field.
An element of the inverse limit is a compatible tuple of classes, each represented by a
polynomial in finitely many of the generators, so countably many coordinates involve only
countably many generators and hence are bounded below `ω₁`. Killing the generators below such a
bound maps the limit onto `ℚ[X]/(X^(n+1))` with `x_α ↦ X` and `y_{αβ} ↦ 1`, and a topologically
nilpotent element of the limit dies there; a finitely generated open ideal would therefore be
killed, while it must contain the `(n+1)`-st power of some `x_γ`, which does not die.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0APW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0APW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AID](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AID)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AIJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AIJ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open Filter Topology

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

universe u

/-- A decreasing sequence of ideals all cutting out a closed subset `T` of the spectrum and
cofinal among the ideals cutting out `T`. This is the ideal-theoretic form of countable
indexedness of the completion of `Spec A` along `T`. -/
abbrev IsCofinalVanishingSequence (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (T : Set (PrimeSpectrum A))
    (J : ℕ → Ideal A) : Prop :=
  (∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) ∧
    (∀ n, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (J n : Set A) = T) ∧
      (∀ K : Ideal A, PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (K : Set A) = T → ∃ n, J n ≤ K)

/-- The inverse limit of the quotients of `A` by a decreasing sequence of ideals, as a subring
of the product of those quotients. -/
def IdealSequenceLimit (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A) (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) :
    Subring (∀ n, A ⧸ J n) where
  carrier := {x | ∀ n m (h : n ≤ m),
    Ideal.Quotient.factor (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ h) (x m) = x n}
  zero_mem' := by simp
  one_mem' := by simp
  add_mem' := by
    intro x y hx hy n m h
    simp [hx n m h, hy n m h]
  mul_mem' := by
    intro x y hx hy n m h
    simp [hx n m h, hy n m h]
  neg_mem' := by
    intro x hx n m h
    change Ideal.Quotient.factor (antitone_nat_of_succ_le hJ h) (-x m) = -x n
    rw [map_neg, hx n m h]

/-- The limit topology on the inverse limit of the quotients, each quotient being discrete. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def idealSequenceLimitTopology (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (J : ℕ → Ideal A)
    (hJ : ∀ n, J (n + 1) ≤ J n) : TopologicalSpace (IdealSequenceLimit A J hJ) :=
  TopologicalSpace.induced Subtype.val
    (@Pi.topologicalSpace ℕ (fun n => A ⧸ J n) (fun _ => ⊥))

/-- The index set of Gabber's example: the first uncountable ordinal, as a type. -/
abbrev GabberIndex.{v} : Type v := (Ordinal.omega.{v} 1).ToType

/-! The algebraic core of Gabber's example has two useful parts.  First,
countably many bounds below `ω₁` have a common bound.  Second, divisibility
propagates a fixed power-membership statement from a cofinal set of indices
to every index. -/

private lemma exists_gabberIndex_gt.{v} {δ : Ordinal.{v}} (hδ : δ < Ordinal.omega.{v} 1) :
    ∃ γ : GabberIndex.{v}, δ < γ.toOrd.val :=
  ⟨Ordinal.ToType.mk ⟨δ + 1, by simpa using (Cardinal.isSuccLimit_omega.{v} 1).succ_lt hδ⟩,
    by simp [Ordinal.ToType.toOrd]⟩

private lemma exists_unbounded_fiber_omega_one
    (f : GabberIndex → ℕ) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, ∀ γ : Ordinal, γ < Ordinal.omega 1 →
      ∃ α : GabberIndex, γ ≤ α.toOrd.val ∧ f α = n := by
  classical
  by_contra h
  push Not at h
  choose b hb hAvoid using h
  obtain ⟨α, hα⟩ := exists_gabberIndex_gt (Ordinal.iSup_lt_omega_one hb)
  exact hAvoid (f α) α ((Ordinal.le_iSup b (f α)).trans_lt hα).le rfl

private lemma powers_mem_of_cofinal_divisibility
    {ι R : Type*} [Preorder ι] [CommRing R]
    (x : ι → R) (I : Ideal R) (n : ℕ) (s : Set ι)
    (hdiv : ∀ i j, i ≤ j → ∃ c : R, x i = c * x j)
    (hcofinal : ∀ i, ∃ j, i ≤ j ∧ j ∈ s)
    (hmem : ∀ j ∈ s, x j ^ n ∈ I) :
    ∀ i, x i ^ n ∈ I := by
  intro i
  obtain ⟨j, hij, hjs⟩ := hcofinal i
  obtain ⟨c, hxi⟩ := hdiv i j hij
  rw [hxi, mul_pow]
  exact I.mul_mem_left _ (hmem j hjs)

private lemma span_powers_le_of_zeroLocus_eq
    {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    (x : GabberIndex → R)
    (K : Ideal R)
    (hdiv : ∀ i j, i ≤ j → ∃ c : R, x i = c * x j)
    (hzero : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus
        (Ideal.span (Set.range x) : Set R) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (K : Set R)) :
    (∃ n : ℕ, 0 < n ∧
      Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i => x i ^ n)) ≤ K) := by
  classical
  have hI : Ideal.span (Set.range x) ≤ K.radical :=
    (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus_subset_zeroLocus_iff K _).mp hzero.ge
  have hpow : ∀ i, ∃ n : ℕ, 0 < n ∧ x i ^ n ∈ K := by
    intro i
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ :=
      Ideal.mem_radical_iff.mp (hI (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self i)))
    exact ⟨n + 1, Nat.succ_pos _,
      Ideal.pow_mem_of_pow_mem (I := K) (a := x i) hn (Nat.le_succ n)⟩
  choose exponent hexponent_pos hexponent using hpow
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := exists_unbounded_fiber_omega_one exponent
  let s : Set GabberIndex :=
    {i | exponent i = n}
  have hcofinal : ∀ i, ∃ j, i ≤ j ∧ j ∈ s := by
    intro i
    obtain ⟨j, hij, hj⟩ := hn i.toOrd.val i.toOrd.property
    exact ⟨j, hij, hj⟩
  have hall : ∀ i, x i ^ n ∈ K :=
    powers_mem_of_cofinal_divisibility x K n s hdiv hcofinal (by
      intro j hj
      rw [← hj]
      exact hexponent j)
  have hnpos : 0 < n := by
    obtain ⟨i, -, hi⟩ := hn 0 (Ordinal.omega_pos 1)
    rw [← hi]
    exact hexponent_pos i
  refine ⟨n, hnpos, Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_⟩
  rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
  exact hall i

private lemma zeroLocus_span_powers
    {ι R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    (x : ι → R) (n : ℕ) (hn : 0 < n) :
    PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus
        (Ideal.span (Set.range (fun i => x i ^ n)) : Set R) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (Ideal.span (Set.range x) : Set R) := by
  ext p
  rw [PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus, PrimeSpectrum.mem_zeroLocus]
  refine ⟨fun hp => Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_, fun hp => Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_⟩
  · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact p.isPrime.mem_of_pow_mem n
      (hp (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self i)))
  · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact p.isPrime.pow_mem_iff_mem n hn |>.2
      (hp (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self i)))

/-- The variables of Gabber's example: one `x_α` for each `α ∈ ω₁` and one `y_{αβ}` for each
pair `α ∈ β ∈ ω₁`. -/
abbrev GabberVariable.{v} : Type v :=
  Sum GabberIndex.{v} (Σ a : GabberIndex.{v},
    {b : GabberIndex.{v} // a.toOrd.val < b.toOrd.val})

/-- The relation `x_α - y_{αβ} x_β` attached to a pair `α ∈ β ∈ ω₁`. -/
def gabberRelationPolynomial.{v}
    (ab : Σ a : GabberIndex.{v}, {b : GabberIndex.{v} // a.toOrd.val < b.toOrd.val}) :
    MvPolynomial GabberVariable.{v} ℚ :=
  MvPolynomial.X (Sum.inl ab.1) -
    MvPolynomial.X (Sum.inr ab) * MvPolynomial.X (Sum.inl ab.2.1)

/-- The ideal generated by the relations `x_α - y_{αβ} x_β`. -/
def gabberRelationIdeal.{v} : Ideal (MvPolynomial GabberVariable.{v} ℚ) :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range gabberRelationPolynomial.{v})

/-- Gabber's ring: the `ℚ`-algebra on the generators `x_α`, `y_{αβ}` subject to the relations
`x_α = y_{αβ} x_β`. -/
abbrev GabberRing.{v} :=
  MvPolynomial GabberVariable.{v} ℚ ⧸ gabberRelationIdeal.{v}

/-- The generator `x_α` of Gabber's ring. -/
def gabberX.{v} (a : GabberIndex.{v}) : GabberRing.{v} :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.X (Sum.inl a))

/-- The generator `y_{αβ}` of Gabber's ring, for `α ∈ β`. -/
def gabberY.{v} (a b : GabberIndex.{v})
    (h : a.toOrd.val < b.toOrd.val) : GabberRing.{v} :=
  Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.X (Sum.inr ⟨a, ⟨b, h⟩⟩))

/-- The defining relation `x_α = y_{αβ} x_β` holds in Gabber's ring. -/
theorem gabberX_eq_gabberY_mul_gabberX.{v}
    (a b : GabberIndex.{v}) (h : a.toOrd.val < b.toOrd.val) :
    gabberX a = gabberY a b h * gabberX b := by
  let ab : Σ a : GabberIndex.{v}, {b : GabberIndex.{v} // a.toOrd.val < b.toOrd.val} :=
    ⟨a, ⟨b, h⟩⟩
  have hab : gabberRelationPolynomial.{v} ab ∈ gabberRelationIdeal.{v} := by
    change gabberRelationPolynomial ab ∈
      Ideal.span (Set.range gabberRelationPolynomial.{v})
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨ab, rfl⟩
  have hzero : Ideal.Quotient.mk gabberRelationIdeal.{v}
      (gabberRelationPolynomial.{v} ab) = 0 :=
    Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hab
  change Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.X (Sum.inl a)) =
    Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.X (Sum.inr ab)) *
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (MvPolynomial.X (Sum.inl b))
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp (by simpa [gabberRelationPolynomial] using hzero)

private lemma later_gabberX_dvd_earlier.{v}
    (a b : GabberIndex.{v}) (h : a ≤ b) :
    ∃ c : GabberRing.{v}, gabberX a = c * gabberX b := by
  have h' : a.toOrd ≤ b.toOrd := (Ordinal.ToType.mk).symm.le_iff_le.mpr h
  have hval : a.toOrd.val ≤ b.toOrd.val := h'
  by_cases hab : a.toOrd.val = b.toOrd.val
  · obtain rfl : a = b := (Ordinal.ToType.mk).symm.injective (Subtype.ext hab)
    exact ⟨1, by simp⟩
  · have hlt : a.toOrd.val < b.toOrd.val := lt_of_le_of_ne hval hab
    exact ⟨gabberY a b hlt, gabberX_eq_gabberY_mul_gabberX a b hlt⟩

/-- The ideal `(x_α : α ∈ ω₁)`, whose zero locus is the closed subset `T` of the example. -/
def gabberVanishingIdeal.{v} : Ideal GabberRing.{v} :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range gabberX.{v})

/-- The ideal `J_n = (x_α^(n+1) : α ∈ ω₁)`; these form the cofinal vanishing sequence for `T`. -/
def gabberPowerIdeal.{v} (n : ℕ) : Ideal GabberRing.{v} :=
  Ideal.span (Set.range fun a : GabberIndex.{v} => gabberX a ^ (n + 1))

/-- Every `J_n` cuts out the same closed subset as `(x_α : α ∈ ω₁)`. -/
theorem gabberPowerIdeal_zeroLocus.{v} (n : ℕ) :
    PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n : Set GabberRing.{v}) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (gabberVanishingIdeal.{v} : Set GabberRing.{v}) :=
  zeroLocus_span_powers gabberX.{v} (n + 1) (Nat.succ_pos _)

/-- The sequence `J_n` is decreasing. -/
theorem gabberPowerIdeal_antitone.{v} (n : ℕ) :
    gabberPowerIdeal.{v} (n + 1) ≤ gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n := by
  apply Ideal.span_le.mpr
  intro z hz
  rcases Set.mem_range.mp hz with ⟨a, rfl⟩
  rw [pow_succ']
  exact (gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n).mul_mem_left _
    (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_range_self a))

private def gabberEvalVariable.{v} (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) :
    GabberVariable.{v} → Polynomial ℚ
  | .inl a => if a.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val then 0 else Polynomial.X
  | .inr ab =>
      if ab.1.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val ∧
          γ.toOrd.val ≤ ab.2.1.toOrd.val then 0 else 1

private def gabberScalarVariable.{v} : GabberVariable.{v} → ℚ
  | .inl _ => 0
  | .inr _ => 1

private lemma gabberRelation_eval.{v} (γ : GabberIndex.{v})
    (ab : Σ a : GabberIndex.{v}, {b : GabberIndex.{v} // a.toOrd.val < b.toOrd.val}) :
    MvPolynomial.aeval (gabberEvalVariable γ) (gabberRelationPolynomial.{v} ab) = 0 := by
  rw [gabberRelationPolynomial, map_sub, map_mul, MvPolynomial.aeval_X,
    MvPolynomial.aeval_X, MvPolynomial.aeval_X]
  dsimp [gabberEvalVariable]
  by_cases h₁ : ab.1.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val
  · by_cases h₂ : γ.toOrd.val ≤ ab.2.1.toOrd.val
    · simp [h₁, h₂]
    · have h₂' : ab.2.1.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val := lt_of_not_ge h₂
      simp [h₁, h₂, h₂']
  · have h₁' : γ.toOrd.val ≤ ab.1.toOrd.val := le_of_not_gt h₁
    have h₂' : ¬ ab.2.1.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val :=
      not_lt_of_ge (le_trans h₁' ab.2.2.le)
    simp [h₁, h₂']

private def gabberEvaluation.{v} (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) :
    GabberRing.{v} →+* Polynomial ℚ :=
  let φ : MvPolynomial GabberVariable.{v} ℚ →+* Polynomial ℚ :=
    (MvPolynomial.aeval (gabberEvalVariable γ)).toRingHom
  Ideal.Quotient.lift gabberRelationIdeal.{v} φ (by
    change Ideal.span (Set.range gabberRelationPolynomial.{v}) ≤ RingHom.ker φ
    refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨ab, rfl⟩
    change MvPolynomial.aeval (gabberEvalVariable γ)
      (gabberRelationPolynomial.{v} ab) = 0
    exact gabberRelation_eval γ ab)

private lemma gabberEvaluation_X_of_below.{v} (γ a : GabberIndex.{v})
    (h : a.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val) : gabberEvaluation γ (gabberX a) = 0 := by
  simp [gabberEvaluation, gabberX, gabberEvalVariable, Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk, h]

private lemma gabberEvaluation_X_of_not_below.{v} (γ a : GabberIndex.{v})
    (h : ¬ a.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val) :
    gabberEvaluation γ (gabberX a) = Polynomial.X := by
  simp [gabberEvaluation, gabberX, gabberEvalVariable, Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk, h]

private def gabberVariableBound.{v} : GabberVariable.{v} → Ordinal
  | .inl a => a.toOrd.val
  | .inr ab => max ab.1.toOrd.val ab.2.1.toOrd.val

private lemma gabberVariableBound_lt.{v} (w : GabberVariable.{v}) :
    gabberVariableBound w < Ordinal.omega.{v} 1 := by
  cases w with
  | inl a => exact a.toOrd.property
  | inr ab => exact max_lt ab.1.toOrd.property ab.2.1.toOrd.property

private lemma gabberFiniteSupport_bound_lt.{v} (s : Finset GabberVariable.{v}) :
    s.sup gabberVariableBound < Ordinal.omega.{v} 1 :=
  (Finset.sup_lt_iff (Ordinal.omega_pos.{v} 1)).2
    (fun w _ => gabberVariableBound_lt w)

private def gabberMonomialBound.{v} (m : GabberVariable.{v} →₀ ℕ) : Ordinal :=
  m.support.sup gabberVariableBound

private def gabberPolynomialBound.{v} (p : MvPolynomial GabberVariable.{v} ℚ) : Ordinal :=
  p.support.sup gabberMonomialBound

private lemma gabberMonomialBound_lt.{v} (m : GabberVariable.{v} →₀ ℕ) :
    gabberMonomialBound m < Ordinal.omega.{v} 1 :=
  gabberFiniteSupport_bound_lt m.support

private lemma gabberPolynomialBound_lt.{v} (p : MvPolynomial GabberVariable.{v} ℚ) :
    gabberPolynomialBound p < Ordinal.omega.{v} 1 :=
  (Finset.sup_lt_iff (Ordinal.omega_pos.{v} 1)).2 fun m _ => gabberMonomialBound_lt m

private noncomputable def gabberRepresentative.{v} (f : GabberRing.{v}) :
    MvPolynomial GabberVariable.{v} ℚ :=
  Classical.choose (Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective f)

private lemma gabberRepresentative_spec.{v} (f : GabberRing.{v}) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk gabberRelationIdeal.{v} (gabberRepresentative f) = f :=
  Classical.choose_spec (Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective f)

private lemma gabberEvaluation_eq_aeval_representative.{v}
    (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) (f : GabberRing.{v}) :
    gabberEvaluation γ f =
      MvPolynomial.aeval (gabberEvalVariable γ) (gabberRepresentative f) := by
  conv_lhs => rw [← gabberRepresentative_spec f]
  simp [gabberEvaluation, Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk]

private lemma exists_bound_gabberRepresentatives.{v} (f : ℕ → GabberRing.{v}) :
    ∃ γ : GabberIndex.{v},
      ∀ n m w, m ∈ (gabberRepresentative (f n)).support → w ∈ m.support →
        gabberVariableBound w < γ.toOrd.val := by
  classical
  let b : ℕ → Ordinal := fun n =>
    gabberPolynomialBound (gabberRepresentative (f n))
  have hb : ∀ n, b n < Ordinal.omega.{v} 1 := fun n =>
    gabberPolynomialBound_lt (gabberRepresentative (f n))
  obtain ⟨γ, hγ⟩ := exists_gabberIndex_gt (Ordinal.iSup_lt_omega_one hb)
  refine ⟨γ, fun n m w hm hw => ?_⟩
  have h₁ : gabberMonomialBound m ≤ b n := Finset.le_sup hm
  have h₂ : gabberVariableBound w ≤ gabberMonomialBound m := Finset.le_sup hw
  exact (h₂.trans h₁).trans (Ordinal.le_iSup b n) |>.trans_lt hγ

private lemma gabberEval_eq_C_scalarEval_of_support_bound.{v}
    (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) (p : MvPolynomial GabberVariable.{v} ℚ)
    (hsupport : ∀ m ∈ p.support, ∀ w ∈ m.support,
      gabberVariableBound w < γ.toOrd.val) :
    MvPolynomial.aeval (gabberEvalVariable γ) p =
      Polynomial.C (MvPolynomial.eval₂ (RingHom.id ℚ) gabberScalarVariable p) := by
  classical
  rw [p.as_sum]
  simp only [map_sum, MvPolynomial.aeval_monomial, MvPolynomial.eval₂_monomial,
    MvPolynomial.eval₂_sum]
  apply Finset.sum_congr rfl
  intro m hm
  have hcoeff :
      (algebraMap ℚ (Polynomial ℚ)) (p.coeff m) =
        Polynomial.C ((RingHom.id ℚ) (p.coeff m)) := by simp
  rw [hcoeff, map_mul]
  congr 1
  rw [map_finsuppProd (Polynomial.C : ℚ →+* Polynomial ℚ) m
    (fun n e => gabberScalarVariable n ^ e)]
  apply Finsupp.prod_congr
  intro w hw
  have hbelow := hsupport m hm w hw
  have heval : gabberEvalVariable γ w = Polynomial.C (gabberScalarVariable w) := by
    cases w with
    | inl a =>
      have ha : a < γ := (Ordinal.ToType.mk).symm.lt_iff_lt.mpr (by
        simpa [gabberVariableBound] using hbelow)
      simp [gabberEvalVariable, gabberScalarVariable, ha]
    | inr ab =>
      have h₁ : ab.1 < γ := (Ordinal.ToType.mk).symm.lt_iff_lt.mpr
        (show ab.1.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val from (le_max_left _ _).trans_lt hbelow)
      have h₂ : ab.2.1 < γ := (Ordinal.ToType.mk).symm.lt_iff_lt.mpr
        (show ab.2.1.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val from (le_max_right _ _).trans_lt hbelow)
      simp [gabberEvalVariable, gabberScalarVariable, h₁, h₂]
  rw [heval, map_pow]

private lemma gabberPowerIdeal_cofinal.{v} (K : Ideal GabberRing.{v})
    (hzero : PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus
        (gabberVanishingIdeal.{v} : Set GabberRing.{v}) =
      PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (K : Set GabberRing.{v})) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n ≤ K := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm, hle⟩ := span_powers_le_of_zeroLocus_eq
    gabberX.{v} K later_gabberX_dvd_earlier.{v} (by simpa [gabberVanishingIdeal] using hzero)
  obtain ⟨n, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_succ_of_ne_zero (Nat.ne_of_gt hm)
  exact ⟨n, by simpa [gabberPowerIdeal] using hle⟩

/-! The quotient sequence has an inverse-limit ring.  Its finite-stage
cutoff evaluations record whether an element sees variables beyond the
chosen ordinal. -/

private abbrev gabberPolynomialTruncation (n : ℕ) :=
  Polynomial ℚ ⧸ Ideal.span ({Polynomial.X ^ (n + 1)} : Set (Polynomial ℚ))

private lemma gabberEvaluationQuotient_ker.{v}
    (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) (n : ℕ) :
    gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n ≤ RingHom.ker
      ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span
        ({Polynomial.X ^ (n + 1)} : Set (Polynomial ℚ)))).comp
        (gabberEvaluation γ)) := by
  refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
  rintro _ ⟨a, rfl⟩
  change Ideal.Quotient.mk _
      (gabberEvaluation γ (gabberX a ^ (n + 1))) = 0
  rw [map_pow]
  by_cases ha : a.toOrd.val < γ.toOrd.val
  · simp [gabberEvaluation_X_of_below γ a ha]
  · rw [gabberEvaluation_X_of_not_below γ a ha]
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.subset_span (by simp))

private noncomputable def gabberEvaluationQuotient.{v}
    (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) (n : ℕ) :
    GabberRing.{v} ⧸ gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n →+* gabberPolynomialTruncation n := by
  exact Ideal.Quotient.lift _ ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span
      ({Polynomial.X ^ (n + 1)} : Set (Polynomial ℚ)))).comp (gabberEvaluation γ))
    (fun x hx => RingHom.mem_ker.mp (gabberEvaluationQuotient_ker γ n hx))

/-- The completion `lim A ⧸ J_n` of Gabber's ring along the sequence `J_n`. -/
abbrev GabberCompletion.{v} :=
  IdealSequenceLimit GabberRing.{v} gabberPowerIdeal.{v}
    gabberPowerIdeal_antitone.{v}

/-- The completion carries the limit topology of the discrete quotients `A ⧸ J_n`. -/
instance gabberCompletionTopologicalSpace.{v} :
    TopologicalSpace GabberCompletion.{v} :=
  idealSequenceLimitTopology GabberRing.{v} gabberPowerIdeal.{v}
    gabberPowerIdeal_antitone.{v}

private noncomputable def gabberCompletionEvaluation.{v}
    (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) (n : ℕ) :
    GabberCompletion.{v} →+* gabberPolynomialTruncation n := by
  refine
    { toFun := fun x => gabberEvaluationQuotient γ n (x.1 n)
      map_one' := ?_
      map_mul' := ?_
      map_zero' := ?_
      map_add' := ?_ }
  all_goals simp

private def gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative.{v}
    (x : GabberCompletion.{v}) (n : ℕ) : GabberRing.{v} :=
  Classical.choose (Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (x.1 n))

private lemma gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative_spec.{v}
    (x : GabberCompletion.{v}) (n : ℕ) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk (gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n)
      (gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative x n) = x.1 n :=
  Classical.choose_spec (Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (x.1 n))

private lemma exists_bound_gabberCompletionRepresentative.{v}
    (x : GabberCompletion.{v}) :
    ∃ γ : GabberIndex.{v}, ∀ n m w,
      m ∈ (gabberRepresentative (gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative x n)).support →
      w ∈ m.support → gabberVariableBound w < γ.toOrd.val :=
  exists_bound_gabberRepresentatives
    (fun n => gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative x n)

private lemma gabberCompletionEvaluation_eq_C_of_bound.{v}
    (x : GabberCompletion.{v}) (γ : GabberIndex.{v})
    (hbound : ∀ n m w,
      m ∈ (gabberRepresentative (gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative x n)).support →
      w ∈ m.support → gabberVariableBound w < γ.toOrd.val)
    (n : ℕ) :
    gabberCompletionEvaluation γ n x =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (Polynomial.C
        (MvPolynomial.eval₂ (RingHom.id ℚ) gabberScalarVariable
          (gabberRepresentative (gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative x n)))) := by
  change gabberEvaluationQuotient γ n (x.1 n) = _
  rw [gabberEvaluationQuotient, ← gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative_spec,
    Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk]
  apply congrArg (Ideal.Quotient.mk _)
  rw [gabberEvaluation_eq_aeval_representative]
  exact gabberEval_eq_C_scalarEval_of_support_bound γ _ fun m hm w hw => hbound n m w hm hw

private def gabberCompletionProjection.{v} (n : ℕ) :
  GabberCompletion.{v} →+* GabberRing.{v} ⧸ gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n :=
  (Pi.evalRingHom (fun n : ℕ => GabberRing.{v} ⧸ gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n) n).comp
    GabberCompletion.subtype

private def gabberCompletionX.{v} (a : GabberIndex.{v}) : GabberCompletion.{v} :=
  ⟨fun n => Ideal.Quotient.mk (gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n) (gabberX a),
    fun n m h => by simp⟩

private lemma gabberPolynomialTruncation_X_pow_ne_zero (n : ℕ) :
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk
      (Ideal.span ({Polynomial.X ^ (n + 2)} : Set (Polynomial ℚ))))
      (Polynomial.X ^ (n + 1)) ≠ 0 := by
  rw [ne_eq, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, Ideal.mem_span_singleton,
    Polynomial.X_pow_dvd_iff]
  intro h
  have hcoeff := h (n + 1) (by omega)
  simp at hcoeff

private lemma gabberCompletionEvaluation_continuous.{v}
    (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) (n : ℕ) :
    @Continuous (GabberCompletion.{v}) (gabberPolynomialTruncation n)
      (idealSequenceLimitTopology GabberRing.{v} gabberPowerIdeal.{v}
        gabberPowerIdeal_antitone.{v})
      ⊥ (gabberCompletionEvaluation.{v} γ n) := by
  let : ∀ k : ℕ, TopologicalSpace
      (GabberRing.{v} ⧸ gabberPowerIdeal.{v} k) := fun _ => ⊥
  let : ∀ k : ℕ, DiscreteTopology
      (GabberRing.{v} ⧸ gabberPowerIdeal.{v} k) := fun _ => ⟨rfl⟩
  let : TopologicalSpace (gabberPolynomialTruncation n) := ⊥
  let : DiscreteTopology (gabberPolynomialTruncation n) := ⟨rfl⟩
  have hcoord : Continuous (fun x : GabberCompletion.{v} => x.1 n) :=
    (continuous_apply n).comp continuous_subtype_val
  change Continuous (fun x : GabberCompletion.{v} =>
    gabberEvaluationQuotient.{v} γ n (x.1 n))
  exact continuous_of_discreteTopology.comp hcoord

private lemma topologicallyNilpotent_isNilpotent_of_discrete
    {R : Type*} [MonoidWithZero R] [TopologicalSpace R] [DiscreteTopology R]
    {x : R} (hx : IsTopologicallyNilpotent x) : IsNilpotent x := by
  unfold IsTopologicallyNilpotent at hx
  have hev : ∀ᶠ n : ℕ in atTop, x ^ n ∈ ({0} : Set R) :=
    hx.eventually ((isOpen_discrete _).mem_nhds rfl)
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hev.exists
  exact ⟨n, by simpa using hn⟩

private lemma polynomialConstant_eq_zero_of_nilpotent_mod_X_power
    (k : ℕ) (hk : 0 < k) (c : ℚ)
    (hc : IsNilpotent
      ((Ideal.Quotient.mk
        (Ideal.span ({Polynomial.X ^ k} : Set (Polynomial ℚ))))
        (Polynomial.C c))) : c = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hc
  have hmem : (Polynomial.C c) ^ m ∈
      Ideal.span ({Polynomial.X ^ k} : Set (Polynomial ℚ)) :=
    Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp (by simpa only [map_pow] using hm)
  have hker : Ideal.span ({Polynomial.X ^ k} : Set (Polynomial ℚ)) ≤
      RingHom.ker (Polynomial.evalRingHom (0 : ℚ)) := by
    refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ rfl
    apply RingHom.mem_ker.mpr
    change Polynomial.eval 0 (Polynomial.X ^ k) = 0
    rw [Polynomial.eval_pow, Polynomial.eval_X]
    exact zero_pow hk.ne'
  have hpow : c ^ m = 0 := by simpa using RingHom.mem_ker.mp (hker hmem)
  exact eq_zero_of_pow_eq_zero hpow

private lemma open_gabberIdeal_contains_coordinate_kernel.{v}
    (I : Ideal GabberCompletion.{v})
    (hI : @IsOpen (GabberCompletion.{v})
      (idealSequenceLimitTopology GabberRing.{v} gabberPowerIdeal.{v}
        gabberPowerIdeal_antitone.{v}) (I : Set GabberCompletion.{v})) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, RingHom.ker (gabberCompletionProjection.{v} n) ≤ I := by
  classical
  let : ∀ n : ℕ, TopologicalSpace
      (GabberRing.{v} ⧸ gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n) := fun _ => ⊥
  have hmem : (I : Set GabberCompletion.{v}) ∈ 𝓝 (0 : GabberCompletion.{v}) :=
    hI.mem_nhds I.zero_mem
  rw [nhds_induced, Filter.mem_comap] at hmem
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hsub⟩ := hmem
  rw [nhds_pi, Filter.mem_pi'] at hU
  obtain ⟨s, t, ht, hpi⟩ := hU
  refine ⟨s.sup id, ?_⟩
  intro x hx
  have hxpi : (x : GabberCompletion.{v}).1 ∈ Set.pi (↑s) t := by
    intro i hi
    have his : i ≤ s.sup id := Finset.le_sup (f := id) hi
    have hcoord : (x : GabberCompletion.{v}).1 i = 0 := by
      have hxcoord : (x : GabberCompletion.{v}).1 (s.sup id) = 0 := by
        change gabberCompletionProjection (s.sup id) x = 0 at hx
        simpa [gabberCompletionProjection] using hx
      have hcompat := (x : GabberCompletion.{v}).2 i (s.sup id) his
      change Ideal.Quotient.factor
          (antitone_nat_of_succ_le gabberPowerIdeal_antitone his)
          ((x : GabberCompletion.{v}).1 (s.sup id)) =
        (x : GabberCompletion.{v}).1 i at hcompat
      rw [hxcoord] at hcompat
      simpa using hcompat.symm
    rw [hcoord]
    exact mem_of_mem_nhds (ht i)
  exact hsub (hpi hxpi)

private lemma exists_bound_gabberCompletionFiniteSet.{v}
    (s : Set GabberCompletion.{v}) (hs : s.Finite) :
    ∃ γ : GabberIndex.{v}, ∀ x ∈ s, ∀ n m w,
      m ∈ (gabberRepresentative (gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative x n)).support →
      w ∈ m.support → gabberVariableBound w < γ.toOrd.val := by
  classical
  choose c hc using exists_bound_gabberCompletionRepresentative.{v}
  let b : GabberCompletion.{v} → Ordinal := fun x => (c x).toOrd.val
  have hδ : hs.toFinset.sup b < Ordinal.omega.{v} 1 :=
    (Finset.sup_lt_iff (Ordinal.omega_pos.{v} 1)).2 fun x _ => (c x).toOrd.property
  obtain ⟨γ, hγ⟩ := exists_gabberIndex_gt hδ
  exact ⟨γ, fun x hx n m w hm hw =>
    (hc x n m w hm hw).trans ((Finset.le_sup (f := b) (hs.mem_toFinset.mpr hx)).trans_lt hγ)⟩

private lemma gabberCompletionEvaluation_eq_zero_of_bounded_topologicallyNilpotent.{v}
    (x : GabberCompletion.{v}) (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) (n : ℕ)
    (hbound : ∀ k m w,
      m ∈ (gabberRepresentative (gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative x k)).support →
      w ∈ m.support → gabberVariableBound w < γ.toOrd.val)
    (htn : IsTopologicallyNilpotent x) :
    gabberCompletionEvaluation.{v} γ n x = 0 := by
  classical
  let : TopologicalSpace (gabberPolynomialTruncation n) := ⊥
  let : DiscreteTopology (gabberPolynomialTruncation n) := ⟨rfl⟩
  have hnil : IsNilpotent (gabberCompletionEvaluation.{v} γ n x) :=
    topologicallyNilpotent_isNilpotent_of_discrete
      (IsTopologicallyNilpotent.map (gabberCompletionEvaluation_continuous.{v} γ n) htn)
  rw [gabberCompletionEvaluation_eq_C_of_bound x γ hbound n] at hnil ⊢
  simp [polynomialConstant_eq_zero_of_nilpotent_mod_X_power (n + 1) n.succ_pos _ hnil]

private lemma gabberCompletion_bounded_generators_le_evaluationKernel.{v}
    (I : Ideal GabberCompletion.{v}) (s : Set GabberCompletion.{v})
    (hspan : I = Ideal.span s) (γ : GabberIndex.{v}) (n : ℕ)
    (hbound : ∀ g ∈ s, ∀ k m w,
      m ∈ (gabberRepresentative (gabberCompletionCoordinateRepresentative g k)).support →
      w ∈ m.support → gabberVariableBound w < γ.toOrd.val)
    (htn : ∀ x ∈ I, IsTopologicallyNilpotent x) :
    I ≤ RingHom.ker (gabberCompletionEvaluation.{v} γ n) := by
  classical
  rw [hspan]
  exact Ideal.span_le.mpr fun g hg => RingHom.mem_ker.mpr <|
    gabberCompletionEvaluation_eq_zero_of_bounded_topologicallyNilpotent g γ n
      (hbound g hg) (htn g (hspan ▸ Ideal.subset_span hg))

/-- **Stacks 0APW (2).** The completion `lim A ⧸ J_n` of Gabber's ring has no finitely
generated weak ideal of definition, hence no finitely generated ideal of definition: it is not
adic with a finitely generated ideal of definition. -/
@[stacks 0APW "clause (2), the example is not adic*, at the level of the ring; the \
sheaf-level form of clause (2) is \
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isCountablyIndexed_not_isAdicStar_gabberCompletionSheaf`"]
theorem gabberCompletion_no_fg_isWeakIdealOfDefinition.{v} :
    ¬ ∃ I : Ideal GabberCompletion.{v},
      I.FG ∧ TopologicalRing.IsWeakIdealOfDefinition I := by
  classical
  rintro ⟨I, hfg, hopen, htn⟩
  obtain ⟨n, hkerI⟩ := open_gabberIdeal_contains_coordinate_kernel I hopen
  obtain ⟨s, hsfinite, hspan'⟩ := Submodule.fg_def.mp hfg
  have hspan : I = Ideal.span s := by simpa only [Ideal.span] using hspan'.symm
  obtain ⟨γ, hbound⟩ := exists_bound_gabberCompletionFiniteSet.{v} s hsfinite
  have hleKer := gabberCompletion_bounded_generators_le_evaluationKernel
    I s hspan γ (n + 1) hbound htn
  have hxker : (gabberCompletionX.{v} γ) ^ (n + 1) ∈
      RingHom.ker (gabberCompletionProjection.{v} n) := by
    rw [RingHom.mem_ker]
    change Ideal.Quotient.mk (gabberPowerIdeal.{v} n)
        (gabberX γ ^ (n + 1)) = 0
    exact Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr (Ideal.subset_span ⟨γ, rfl⟩)
  have hevalX : gabberCompletionEvaluation.{v} γ (n + 1)
      (gabberCompletionX.{v} γ) =
        Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (Polynomial.X : Polynomial ℚ) := by
    change gabberEvaluationQuotient.{v} γ (n + 1)
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (gabberPowerIdeal.{v} (n + 1)) (gabberX γ)) = _
    simp [gabberEvaluationQuotient, RingHom.comp_apply, Ideal.Quotient.lift_mk,
      gabberEvaluation_X_of_not_below γ γ (by simp)]
  have hzero := RingHom.mem_ker.mp (hleKer (hkerI hxker))
  rw [map_pow, hevalX] at hzero
  exact gabberPolynomialTruncation_X_pow_ne_zero n hzero

/-- **Stacks 0APW (2).** The ideals `J_n = (x_α^(n+1))` decrease, all cut out
`T = V(x_α : α ∈ ω₁)`, and are cofinal among the ideals cutting out `T`; so the completion of
`Spec A` along `T` is countably indexed. -/
@[stacks 0APW "clause (2), the example is countably indexed, as cofinality of the ideal \
sequence; the sheaf-level form of clause (2) is \
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.isCountablyIndexed_not_isAdicStar_gabberCompletionSheaf`"]
theorem isCofinalVanishingSequence_gabberPowerIdeal.{v} :
    IsCofinalVanishingSequence GabberRing.{v}
      (PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (gabberVanishingIdeal.{v} : Set GabberRing.{v}))
      gabberPowerIdeal.{v} :=
  ⟨gabberPowerIdeal_antitone, gabberPowerIdeal_zeroLocus,
    fun K hK => gabberPowerIdeal_cofinal K hK.symm⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace

